# Copy to .env.local and fill from `supabase status` (local) or the project dashboard.
#
# ⚠ These values are CASE-SENSITIVE. A host panel or CI that normalises env values
# to upper case will produce `SB_PUBLISHABLE_…`, which Supabase rejects with
# `401 {"message":"Invalid API key"}` on every request — the site then loads but
# shows an empty catalog. src/lib/supabaseConfig.ts validates the format and falls
# back to the checked-in public values rather than shipping a dead client, but the
# deploy environment should still be correct.
#
# Both values are public by design (RLS is the security boundary). Never put a
# service_role / sb_secret_ key here — it would ship to every browser.
VITE_SUPABASE_URL=
VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=
